{%- comment -%}
  The 12 questions — ONE dynamic screen, matching the approved Claude
  Design export's own architecture (a single parameterized `question`
  screen driven by a `step` index, not 12 near-duplicate screens). Copy,
  options and kind (text / single-select / multi-select) for each of the
  12 steps live in the QUESTIONS array in assets/pet-health-profile.js and
  are rendered into the containers below at runtime; see that file for the
  exact wording ported from the design.

  Autosave: assets/pet-health-profile.js calls save-progress after every
  answered Continue — data-vphp-saving / data-vphp-save-error are not in
  the approved mockup (which has no backend to fail against) but are
  required so a failed autosave is visible rather than silently lost.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="vphp__screen" data-vphp-screen="question" hidden aria-labelledby="vphp-q-h">
  <div class="vphp__col vphp__col--narrow" data-vphp-col>
    <div class="vphp__progress">
      <div class="vphp__progress-row">
        <span class="vphp__progress-label" data-vphp-field="q.stepLabel">Question 1 of 12</span>
        <span class="vphp__progress-pct" data-vphp-field="q.stepPct">8%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="vphp__progress-track">
        <div class="vphp__progress-fill" data-vphp-bar style="width:8%;"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h1 class="vphp__h1 vphp__h1--q" id="vphp-q-h" data-vphp-field="q.title">What is your pet's name?</h1>
    <p class="vphp__q-sub" data-vphp-field="q.sub">Everything after this is written for them by name.</p>

    <div data-vphp-qcontent></div>

    <p class="vphp__multi-hint" data-vphp-multi-hint hidden>Select all that apply.</p>

    <div class="vphp__save-row">
      <span class="vphp__saving" data-vphp-saving hidden>Saving&hellip;</span>
      <p class="vphp__save-error" data-vphp-save-error hidden role="alert">
        Couldn't save your last answer. Check your connection and try again.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="vphp__footbar" data-vphp-chrome>
    <div class="vphp__footinner">
      <button type="button" class="vphp__btn vphp__btn--outline vphp__btn--foot" data-vphp-act="back">Back</button>
      <button type="button" class="vphp__btn vphp__btn--primary vphp__btn--foot" data-vphp-act="next" disabled>Continue</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
